dex-attachments">Copy Name</button></div></summary><div class="cmd-body"><div class="cmd-body-inner"><div class="cmd-warn">⚠️ Read the "Wire spike results" section in <code>plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md</code> first — it documents the chosen InputItem shape for images per the codex 0.125 spike.</div><pre class="cmd-pre">/plan-with-ralph &quot;Gap 3 from plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md — image attachments never reach codex turn input. Today packages/happy-cli/src/codex/runCodex.ts:321 calls messageQueue.push(message.content.text, ...) — message.content.attachments is read NOWHERE on the codex path, and sendTurnAndWait (codexAppServerClient.ts:1338-1341) hardcodes input as `[{ type: &#x27;text&#x27;, text: prompt }]`. The wire InputItem (codexAppServerTypes.ts:134-137) DOES support image inputs — happy-cli just never produces them. PREREQUISITE: codex-wire-spike must have landed and answered whether codex accepts InputItem `{ type: &#x27;image&#x27;, url: &#x27;data:image/png;base64,...&#x27; }` (preferred — no tmpfile management) or requires `{ type: &#x27;localImage&#x27;, path }` (needs tmpfile write + cleanup). Fix: plumb MessageQueueAttachment[] through MessageQueue2&#x27;s payload to runCodex.ts&#x27;s main loop (mirror the Claude path&#x27;s claudeRemote.ts:65-90 `toClaudeUserContent`), synthesize InputItem[] in sendTurnAndWait based on the spike&#x27;s chosen wire shape. Support PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP (same set as Claude); skip + log unsupported MIME types. Acceptance: integration test sends a PNG attachment end-to-end against a mocked codex app-server; codex agent acknowledges the image content. Cross-package typecheck green. Test command: pnpm --filter &#x27;{packages/happy-cli}&#x27; exec vitest run 2&gt;&amp;1 | tee /tmp/codexu-attachments.log. Single commit; update plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md Gap 3 section to mark shipped.&quot;</pre></div></div></details><details class="cmd" id="cmd-codex-plan-mode-defensive" data-task-id="codex-plan-mode-defensive" data-task-scope="codexu" data-task-phase="plan-ready" data-task-status="blocked" data-cmd-status="ready" data-workstream="codex-parity" data-size-bucket="small" data-cadence="one-shot"><summary><input type="checkbox" class="cmd-select" aria-label="Select codex-plan-mode-defensive for bulk copy" readOnly=""/><span class="cmd-name">codex-plan-mode-defensive</span><span class="cmd-scope-cluster"><span class="task-scope-chip codexu" title="Codexu-side worktree preamble injected at Copy time (.worktrees/&lt;task-id&gt;/ on ralph/&lt;task-id&gt;).">🟦 codexu</span><span class="cmd-badge b-plan-ready">📋 plan ready</span><span class="cmd-status-mod blocked">blocked</span></span><span class="cmd-desc">Gap 6 — defensive plan-mode mapping on codex path (v1, ~2h). V2 overlay-crate deferred. Spawned by <code>codex-parity-audit</code>.</span><a class="pill-workstream" href="#" data-workstream="codex-parity" title="Filter to Codex parity workstream (size: small)">Codex parity</a><a class="pill-spawned-from" href="#cmd-codex-parity-audit" title="Spawned from codex-parity-audit (click to jump)"><span class="from-arrow">↗</span>from codex-parity-audit</a><span class="quick-actions" aria-label="Quick actions for codex-plan-mode-defensive"><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy markdown link for codex-plan-mode-defensive" title="Copy markdown link">🔗</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy ID and status for codex-plan-mode-defensive" title="Copy ID and status">#</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to parent codex-parity-audit" title="Jump to parent codex-parity-audit">↑</button></span><div class="cmd-actions"><button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Command</button><button type="button" class="copy-name-btn" title="Copy task name &quot;codex-plan-mode-defensive&quot; to clipboard" data-copy-text="codex-plan-mode-defensive">Copy Name</button></div></summary><div class="cmd-body"><div class="cmd-body-inner"><div class="cmd-warn blocked">🔒 Operator-gated. Per <code>plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md</code> Gap 6 — two-tier choice: (a) defensive parity now (map <code>plan</code> → codex <code>read-only</code> sandbox + UX hint that ExitPlanMode isn't available, ~2h) OR (b) full parity via a new overlay crate <code>codex/codex-rs-overlay/codex-plan-mode/</code> that injects an <code>exit_plan_mode</code> tool (Medium-to-Large, spike upstream codex's tool-registration seam first). Decide before scoping. Audit recommended (a) for v1.</div><pre class="cmd-pre">/plan-with-ralph &quot;Gap 6 from plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md — defensive plan-mode mapping on codex path. Today packages/happy-cli/src/codex/cliArgs.ts VALID_CODEX_REMOTE_PERMISSION_MODES (re-exported as VALID_REMOTE_PERMISSION_MODES in runCodex.ts:251) is restricted to default, read-only, safe-yolo, yolo — `plan` arriving from the mobile UI is silently ignored (runCodex.ts:287-294); the local CLI flag path falls into the defensive branch in executionPolicy.ts:24,39 returning untrusted+workspace-write. There is no ExitPlanMode codex tool. PREREQUISITE (operator-gated): confirm v1 scope is option (a) DEFENSIVE — map `plan` → codex `read-only` sandbox in executionPolicy.ts, AND emit a UI hint (session-event &#x27;message&#x27;) on first plan-mode entry: &#x27;Plan mode on codex is approximated as read-only; ExitPlanMode tool is not available.&#x27; If operator wants option (b) overlay-crate full parity instead, defer this task and open a separate `codex-plan-mode-overlay` ralph command that lands an overlay crate codex/codex-rs-overlay/codex-plan-mode/ providing real plan-mode parity (model gets an exit_plan_mode tool, mode transitions on tool call) — spike upstream codex&#x27;s tool-registration seam first. Acceptance for v1 (a): switching a codex session to plan mode results in sandbox: read-only, approvalPolicy: never, and the user sees the explanatory message; the existing mobile-UI plan-mode badge still renders correctly. Cross-package typecheck green. Test command: pnpm --filter &#x27;{packages/happy-cli}&#x27; exec vitest run 2&gt;&amp;1 | tee /tmp/codexu-plan-mode.log. Single commit referencing audit Gap 6. Update plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md Gap 6 section to mark v1-defensive shipped; flag v2-overlay as still deferred. Workflow: codexu worktree at .worktrees/codex-plan-mode-defensive/ on topic branch ralph/codex-plan-mode-defensive off origin/main.&quot;</pre></div></div></details><details class="cmd" id="cmd-agent-tree-rpc" data-task-id="agent-tree-rpc" data-task-scope="codexu" data-task-phase="shipped" data-task-status="ok" data-cmd-status="shipped" data-workstream="agent-arch" data-size-bucket="medium" data-cadence="one-shot"><summary><input type="checkbox" class="cmd-select" aria-label="Select agent-tree-rpc for bulk copy" readOnly=""/><span class="cmd-name">agent-tree-rpc</span><span class="cmd-scope-cluster"><span class="task-scope-chip codexu" title="Codexu-side worktree preamble injected at Copy time (.worktrees/&lt;task-id&gt;/ on ralph/&lt;task-id&gt;).">🟦 codexu</span><span class="cmd-badge b-shipped">✅ shipped</span></span><span class="cmd-desc">App-server RPC exposing codex's live spawn tree (sessionGetAgentTree + agent-tree-update events). Spawned by <code>agent-view-research</code>. Branch <code>agent-tree-rpc</code>.</span><a class="pill-workstream" href="#" data-workstream="agent-arch" title="Filter to Agent architecture workstream (size: medium)">Agent architecture</a><a class="pill-spawned-from" href="#cmd-agent-view-research" title="Spawned from agent-view-research (click to jump)"><span class="from-arrow">↗</span>from agent-view-research</a><span class="quick-actions" aria-label="Quick actions for agent-tree-rpc"><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy markdown link for agent-tree-rpc" title="Copy markdown link">🔗</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy ID and status for agent-tree-rpc" title="Copy ID and status">#</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to parent agent-view-research" title="Jump to parent agent-view-research">↑</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to first child codex-child-spawn-tools of agent-tree-rpc" title="Jump to first child codex-child-spawn-tools">↓1</button></span><div class="cmd-actions"><button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Command</button><button type="button" class="copy-name-btn" title="Copy task name &quot;agent-tree-rpc&quot; to clipboard" data-copy-text="agent-tree-rpc">Copy Name</button></div></summary><div class="cmd-body"><div class="cmd-body-inner"><pre class="cmd-pre">/plan-with-ralph &quot;Expose codex&#x27;s live spawn tree as a queryable + streamable app-server RPC. Per plans/agent-view-research.md §6 task `agent-tree-rpc`. Today codex already has the data — AgentRegistry.agent_tree (codex/external/repos/codex-patched/codex-rs/core/src/agent/registry.rs), control.rs:832-840 subscribe_status, and CollabAgentSpawnBegin/EndEvent are emitted (spawn.rs:71-205) — but nothing exposes the live tree as a single queryable surface that mobile clients can render. Minimize-conflict-surface tenet per plans/codexu-roadmap.md: codex source READ-ONLY; add the RPC bridge on the happy-cli side (packages/happy-cli/src/codex/codexAppServerClient.ts + runCodex.ts) by subscribing to codex&#x27;s existing event stream and re-emitting structured spawn-tree updates over happy-server&#x27;s Socket.IO. Add two RPC shapes: (1) sessionGetAgentTree(sessionId) → { nodes: AgentTreeNode[], edges: { parent, child }[] } where AgentTreeNode = { threadId, agentRole, nickname, status, lastTaskMessage, spawnedAt }; (2) socket subscription event &#x27;agent-tree-update&#x27; emitting incremental deltas (node-added, node-status-changed, node-removed). Read codex/external/repos/codex-patched/codex-rs/core/src/agent/registry.rs + control.rs (READ-ONLY) for the data shape. Read packages/happy-cli/src/codex/runCodex.ts for the existing codex event subscription pattern. Read packages/happy-server/sources/app/events/eventRouter.ts for the fan-out primitive. Acceptance: codex spawns 2 sub-agents via spawn_agent → happy-cli detects + emits agent-tree-update events → happy-server fans out → vitest assertion that subscribed clients receive both spawn-begin and spawn-end deltas in correct order with parent linkage. Cross-package typecheck green. Single commit on main, NO codex submodule edits. Pitfall: subscribe_status returns a tokio watch::Receiver that lives in codex&#x27;s process — happy-cli&#x27;s bridge must hold the receiver in a task that survives across the agent&#x27;s lifetime, not just for one tool call.&quot;</pre><div class="run-history"><div class="run-history-label">Run history — 1 run</div><div class="run-entry outcome-completed"><span class="run-date">2026-05-13</span><span class="run-sha">4f5762f9</span><span class="run-summary">Shipped agent-tree RPC plumbing on branch agent-tree-rpc: shared wire schemas, happy-cli reducer and sessionGetAgentTree RPC, live agent-tree-update delta emission, Codex v2/legacy spawn-event parsing, and happy-server validation plus session/user-scoped fan-out. Real-Codex nested child acceptance remains blocked by child-agent tool availability.</span></div></div><div class="spawned-children"><span class="sc-label">Spawned follow-ups (1)</span><a class="sc-chip" href="#cmd-codex-child-spawn-tools" title="Jump to codex-child-spawn-tools">codex-child-spawn-tools</a></div></div></div></details><details class="cmd" id="cmd-agent-status-stream" data-task-id="agent-status-stream" data-task-scope="codexu" data-task-phase="plan-ready" data-task-status="ok" data-cmd-status="ready" data-workstream="agent-arch" data-size-bucket="large" data-cadence="one-shot"><summary><input type="checkbox" class="cmd-select" aria-label="Select agent-status-stream for bulk copy" readOnly=""/><span class="cmd-name">agent-status-stream</span><span class="cmd-scope-cluster"><span class="task-scope-chip codexu" title="Codexu-side worktree preamble injected at Copy time (.worktrees/&lt;task-id&gt;/ on ralph/&lt;task-id&gt;).">🟦 codexu</span><span class="cmd-badge b-plan-ready">📋 plan ready</span></span><span class="cmd-desc">Live "active teammates" overlay in app — bridges shipped agent-tree-update events through happy-cli/server to mobile. Spawned by <code>agent-view-research</code>.</span><a class="pill-workstream" href="#" data-workstream="agent-arch" title="Filter to Agent architecture workstream (size: large)">Agent architecture</a><a class="pill-spawned-from" href="#cmd-agent-view-research" title="Spawned from agent-view-research (click to jump)"><span class="from-arrow">↗</span>from agent-view-research</a><span class="quick-actions" aria-label="Quick actions for agent-status-stream"><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy markdown link for agent-status-stream" title="Copy markdown link">🔗</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy ID and status for agent-status-stream" title="Copy ID and status">#</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to parent agent-view-research" title="Jump to parent agent-view-research">↑</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to kanban card for agent-status-stream" title="Jump to kanban card">◫</button></span><div class="cmd-actions"><button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Command</button><button type="button" class="copy-name-btn" title="Copy task name &quot;agent-status-stream&quot; to clipboard" data-copy-text="agent-status-stream">Copy Name</button></div></summary><div class="cmd-body"><div class="cmd-body-inner"><pre class="cmd-pre">/plan-with-ralph &quot;Bridge codex&#x27;s per-session spawn-tree updates from agent-tree-rpc through to a live &#x27;active teammates&#x27; overlay in the happy-app session detail view. Per plans/agent-view-research.md §6 task `agent-status-stream`. PREREQUISITE: agent-tree-rpc must have landed so happy-server emits &#x27;agent-tree-update&#x27; events with structured deltas. happy-app side: (1) sources/sync/storage.ts — add agentTreeBySession: Record&lt;sid, AgentTreeNode[]&gt; reducer state; subscribe to agent-tree-update events via the existing socket plumbing; apply deltas with a per-session monotonic guard using the shipped delta.seq field (server frames are { sessionId, delta }). (2) sources/app/(app)/session/[id].tsx — add a collapsible &#x27;Active teammates&#x27; overlay panel showing the spawn tree (parent thread + spawned sub-agents) with live status indicators (&#x27;running&#x27; / &#x27;idle&#x27; / &#x27;completed&#x27; / &#x27;failed&#x27; pulsed dot); tap a teammate row to peek its last-task-message + lastN messages (separate RPC, follow-up). Reuse mobile-tree-view&#x27;s depth-indentation pattern for the teammate sub-tree rendering. Read packages/happy-app/CLAUDE.md sync invariants — the new reducer state is in-memory only (ephemeral; don&#x27;t persist to MMKV); reconnect should re-fetch full tree via sessionGetAgentTree(sid) once and then resume incremental deltas. Acceptance: integration test — happy-cli emits &#x27;agent-tree-update&#x27; with 2 spawn events, app receives both, panel shows 2 teammates with correct status; status transition to &#x27;completed&#x27; updates the panel pulsed dot. Cross-package typecheck green. ONE commit per side (happy-app commit; happy-cli changes minimal since agent-tree-rpc already lands the wire shape). Pitfall: subscribe_status&#x27;s watch::Receiver fires aggressively (every internal state tick); happy-cli&#x27;s bridge must coalesce to status-changed deltas only — verify the bridge dedupes idempotent re-emissions before fanning out to clients. Surface UX choice to operator BEFORE building: should the &#x27;Active teammates&#x27; overlay auto-show when a session has &gt; 0 children, or only after user opens it from a menu?&quot;</pre></div></div></details><details class="cmd" id="cmd-codex-child-spawn-tools" data-task-id="codex-child-spawn-tools" data-task-scope="codexu" data-task-phase="plan-ready" data-task-status="ok" data-cmd-status="ready" data-workstream="agent-arch" data-size-bucket="small" data-cadence="one-shot"><summary><input type="checkbox" class="cmd-select" aria-label="Select codex-child-spawn-tools for bulk copy" readOnly=""/><span class="cmd-name">codex-child-spawn-tools</span><span class="cmd-scope-cluster"><span class="task-scope-chip codexu" title="Codexu-side worktree preamble injected at Copy time (.worktrees/&lt;task-id&gt;/ on ralph/&lt;task-id&gt;).">🟦 codexu</span><span class="cmd-badge b-plan-ready">📋 plan ready</span></span><span class="cmd-desc">Spike: do codex child agents get <code>spawn_agent</code>/<code>wait_agent</code> in their tool surface? Decision input for plugin-scope-agents + agent-comms. Spawned by <code>agent-tree-rpc</code> (US-006 AC4 gap).</span><a class="pill-workstream" href="#" data-workstream="agent-arch" title="Filter to Agent architecture workstream (size: small)">Agent architecture</a><a class="pill-spawned-from" href="#cmd-agent-tree-rpc" title="Spawned from agent-tree-rpc (click to jump)"><span class="from-arrow">↗</span>from agent-tree-rpc</a><span class="quick-actions" aria-label="Quick actions for codex-child-spawn-tools"><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy markdown link for codex-child-spawn-tools" title="Copy markdown link">🔗</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy ID and status for codex-child-spawn-tools" title="Copy ID and status">#</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Jump to parent agent-tree-rpc" title="Jump to parent agent-tree-rpc">↑</button></span><div class="cmd-actions"><button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Command</button><button type="button" class="copy-name-btn" title="Copy task name &quot;codex-child-spawn-tools&quot; to clipboard" data-copy-text="codex-child-spawn-tools">Copy Name</button></div></summary><div class="cmd-body"><div class="cmd-body-inner"><pre class="cmd-pre">/plan-with-ralph &quot;Investigation spike — surfaced by agent-tree-rpc&#x27;s unmet US-006 AC4 (commit 11bc1ff4; see plans/overview-data.js OVERVIEW_DATA.runs[] filtered to taskId=&#x27;agent-tree-rpc&#x27;). The agent-tree-rpc agent tried to test nested A→B spawn (codex top-level spawns child, child spawns grandchild) and discovered the pinned codex submodule does NOT expose spawn_agent / wait_agent in child agents&#x27; tool surface. Investigate: (1) Is this an upstream codex design choice or an artifact of the pinned version? Look in codex/external/repos/codex-patched/codex-rs/multi_agents_v2/ for the tool-registration site (spawn.rs + the parent/child role distinction). (2) If upstream HEAD exposes these tools to children, recommend a submodule bump (and surface scope to operator). If not, design an overlay crate (codex/codex-rs-overlay/codex-child-spawn-tools/?) that enables them — sketch the registration seam + permission-profile implications. (3) Decision context: does codexu&#x27;s roadmap actually need child→grandchild spawning, or is top-level-only spawning sufficient? Cross-reference plans/agent-view-research.md §6 (the agent-view-research follow-ups assume parent→child works) and plans/codexu-roadmap.md §Phase 2c (plugin-scope-agents) — if plugin-scope-agents adopts the agent-spawner pattern (one designated top-level agent spawns top-level sessions for the operator), child-spawn-tools may be unnecessary; if agent-comms Scope C (parent-spawned-child) needs in-session spawning, child-spawn-tools is required. Output: new doc plans/codex-child-spawn-tools.md with (a) factual findings (what upstream codex does, what pinned codex does, where the divergence is), (b) decision matrix for our roadmap (top-level-only vs child-can-spawn — affects plugin-scope-agents AND agent-comms scope), (c) recommended path (bump, overlay, or accept). Surface to operator BEFORE plugin-scope-agents fires — plugin-scope-agents is currently parallel-safe but its scoping model depends on this. NO code changes — research only. The ralph job for this spike should NOT require codex-submodule edits; reading is fine. ~2-4h.&quot;</pre></div></div></details><details class="cmd" id="cmd-port-explorer-prompt" data-task-id="port-explorer-prompt" data-task-scope="codex" data-task-phase="shipped" data-task-status="ok" data-merge-commit="e9fa64a0,d279d49d" data-cmd-status="shipped" data-workstream="agent-arch" data-size-bucket="small" data-cadence="one-shot"><summary><input type="checkbox" class="cmd-select" aria-label="Select port-explorer-prompt for bulk copy" readOnly=""/><span class="cmd-name">port-explorer-prompt</span><span class="cmd-scope-cluster"><span class="task-scope-chip codex" title="Codex-submodule worktree preamble injected at Copy time (.ralph/jobs/&lt;task-id&gt;/codex-worktree/).">🦀 codex</span><span class="cmd-badge b-shipped">✅ shipped</span></span><span class="cmd-desc">Filled empty <code>explorer.toml</code> stub with paraphrased Explore prompt · codex commit <code>e9fa64a0</code> · codexu pointer-bump <code>d279d49d</code>. Spawned by <code>native-agent-parity</code>.</span><a class="pill-workstream" href="#" data-workstream="agent-arch" title="Filter to Agent architecture workstream (size: small)">Agent architecture</a><a class="pill-spawned-from" href="#cmd-native-agent-parity" title="Spawned from native-agent-parity (click to jump)"><span class="from-arrow">↗</span>from native-agent-parity</a><span class="quick-actions" aria-label="Quick actions for port-explorer-prompt"><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy markdown link for port-explorer-prompt" title="Copy markdown link">🔗</button><button type="button" class="quick-action-btn" aria-label="Copy ID and status for port-explorer-prompt" title="Copy ID and status">#<